    pr_ref:  # 2d35
    description: "Deferred precision follow-up of WI-noham Part A (PR #404). Part A's receiver_type_hint carries only the class NAME; the inherited_calls linker re-globalizes it via class_ids_by_name and, for non-legacy languages, biases to unresolved when two in-repo classes share that short name (the len(type_class_ids)>1 ambiguity guard — INV-fahub-airtight but sacrifices recall). py.py already holds the concrete class Symbol (var_types[recv].id / .path), so threading a concrete class-id (or (path,name)) alongside the name would let the linker resolve the collision case precisely instead of dropping it — recovering the recall the ambiguity guard sacrifices, and closing the INV-fahub-spirit residual outright (a class-name hint that re-globalizes is a mild information-loss). Requires extending make_unresolved_edge / the Site-2 meta contract to carry a concrete class ref, and the inherited_calls dispatch to prefer it over the name. Lower priority than D1/D2 (precision refinement, not a coverage gap)."  # 2d35
    fields: {}  # 2d35
